INF1103 PROJECT
AI-BASED HEALTHCARE ERROR LOGGING SYSTEM
Domain: Healthcare
Topic: Error Logging
GitHub: https://github.com/INF1103-Team-2/Project.git

01 — PROBLEM:
    Healthcare machines can generate a large number of error logs during operation. These logs may contain different error codes, machine information, timestamps, and descriptions.
    Manually reviewing large amounts of error logs can be time-consuming and makes it difficult to quickly identify which issues require attention.
    Our Goal:
        To develop an AI-based error logging system that can:
            Process raw machine error logs
            Sort and categorize errors
            Identify potential anomalies
            Determine error severity
            Automatically report relevant errors to engineers

02 — TARGET USERS:
    Hospital Staff
    Upload and review machine error logs.
    Engineers
    Receive notifications about machine errors that require attention.
    Operators
    Monitor machine errors and receive relevant updates.

03 — USER INPUT:
    Raw Machine Error Logs
    Users upload error log files through the application.
    The logs may contain:
    Machine ID
    Timestamp
    Error Code
    Error Description
    Machine Status
    Sensor Readings
    Example
    2026-09-16 21:30:05 | MACHINE_001 | E102 | Temperature exceeded 90°C

04—OUR SOLUTION:
IO MANAGER - Zoey
    Handles user input and file uploads.
    Upload raw error logs
    Read and validate files
    Pass raw data to AI Manager

AI ANALYSIS MANAGER - Jing Jie • Owen
    Uses AI to process and organize the error logs.
    Analyze raw logs
    Extract important information
    Sort and categorize errors
    Detect potential anomalies
    Determine error severity
    Convert logs into structured data

LOGIC MANAGER - Jia Yi • Naim
    Determines what action should be taken.
    Receive processed data
    Check error severity
    Apply notification rules
    Decide when notifications should be sent
    Send information to Telegram API

DATA MANAGER - Su Bin
    Stores processed information using JSON files.
    Store error logs
    Store machine information
    Store error details
    Store severity and notification status

05 — HOW AI IS USED:
    RAW LOG
    MACHINE_001 | E102 | Temperature exceeded 90°C
    ↓
    AI ANALYSIS
    The AI identifies:
    Machine: MACHINE_001
    Error Code: E102
    Error Type: Temperature
    Severity: URGENT
    ↓
    STRUCTURED DATA
    {
    "machine_id": "MACHINE_001",
    "error_code": "E102",
    "error_type": "Temperature",
    "severity": "URGENT"
    }
    The AI focuses on:
    “What is happening?”
    The logic manager then determines:
    “What should we do?”
06 — TELEGRAM API:
    The Telegram API is used as our main method of error reporting and notification.
    After the logic manager processes an error, the system sends the relevant information to a Telegram bot.
    Example Notification
    🚨 URGENT MACHINE ERROR
    Machine: MACHINE_001
    Error Code: E102
    Error Type: Temperature
    Severity: URGENT
    Temperature exceeded the allowed threshold.
    Action Required: Immediate inspection.
    This allows engineers to receive clear and structured information without manually searching through large numbers of error logs.

07 — ERROR SCENARIOS:
    SCENARIO A — URGENT ERROR
    When an error is classified as URGENT, the system immediately notifies the engineer.
    RAW LOG
    ↓
    IO MANAGER
    ↓
    AI ANALYSIS
    ↓
    URGENT ERROR
    ↓
    LOGIC MANAGER
    ↓
    TELEGRAM API
    ↓
    ENGINEER
    SCENARIO B — NON-URGENT ERROR
    When an error is classified as NON-URGENT, the system stores the error and delays the notification.
    The notification will be sent during the designated reporting period, such as after 7:00 AM.
    RAW LOG
    ↓
    IO MANAGER
    ↓
    AI ANALYSIS
    ↓
    NON-URGENT ERROR
    ↓
    STORE / QUEUE
    ↓
    AFTER 7:00 AM
    ↓
    TELEGRAM API
    ↓
    ENGINEER

08 — SYSTEM FLOW:
    MACHINE ERROR LOGS
    ↓
    IO MANAGER
    The user uploads the raw log.
    ↓
    AI MANAGER
    Sort • Categorise • Analyze • Detect Anomalies
    ↓
    LOGIC MANAGER
    Check Severity • Apply Rules • Decide Notification
    ↓
    TELEGRAM API
    ↓
    ENGINEER
    DATA MANAGER
    Processed information is stored in JSON format throughout the process.

09 — EXPECTED OUTCOME:
    Our system aims to:
    Reduce manual error-log processing
    Organize large amounts of error data
    Use AI to identify and categorize errors
    Detect potential machine anomalies
    Identify error severity
    Store processed data in JSON
    Immediately notify engineers about urgent errors
    Delay non-urgent notifications until the appropriate time
    Provide engineers with clear and structured error information through Telegram
KEY IDEA:
    RAW ERROR LOGS → AI → LOGIC → TELEGRAM → ENGINEER
    Using AI to understand and organize the errors, logic to decide what happens next, and Telegram to communicate the results.
